<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=eyeglasses">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eyeglasses</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1290</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eyeglasses, or spectacles, are lenses held in a frame in front of the eyes; the first are estimated to have been made in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, most likely in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, by about 1290. In a sermon of 23 February 1306 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican friar</a> Giordano da Pisa said the art had been found less than twenty years before. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> soon became a centre of manufacture using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murano">Murano</a> glass, and by 1301 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guild</a> regulations there governed their sale. The earliest surviving examples, found at Kloster Wienhausen in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, date from about 1400.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eyeglasses.jpg" alt="Eyeglasses" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Conrad von Soest · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conrad_von_Soest,_'Brillenapostel'_(1403).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 1290</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Pisa or Florence, Italy</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>A 17th-century claim that Salvino degli Armati of Florence invented them is false, and the suggested Chinese and Indian origins rest on later evidence.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/glassmaking">Glassmaking<span>c. 2500 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-optics">Book of Optics<span>1011–1021</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/telescope">Telescope<span>1608</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/microscope">Microscope<span>c. 1620</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=eyeglasses">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
